From 51f483435046face707fa98a1c73d99a11be4a4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manus AI <manus@reai.dev>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 06:13:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix PACER adapter: proper authentication flow with
 X-NEXT-GEN-CSO token

- Rewrote pacer_bankruptcy.py to use correct PACER PCL API auth flow:
  1. Authenticate via POST to pacer.login.uscourts.gov/services/cso-auth
  2. Use returned nextGenCSO token in X-NEXT-GEN-CSO header for searches
  3. POST to pcl.uscourts.gov/pcl-public-api/rest/parties/find with proper JSON body
- Fixed 406 error: was using basic auth instead of token-based auth
- Added jurisdictionType='bk' and GA court IDs filter to party search
- Made FEMA optional in pipeline (skip by default since leads lack lat/lon)
- Added graceful healthcheck error handling in app.py
- Added .gitignore for pycache, .env, and output files
- Added convert_leads.py for Excel-to-CSV conversion
- Added test scripts for PACER auth and search verification
- Removed tracked __pycache__ files
