index 0000000..9744532
--- /dev/null
+++ b/pacer_api_notes.md
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# PACER PCL API Notes
+
+## Authentication
+- POST to: https://pacer.login.uscourts.gov/services/cso-auth
+- Content-Type: application/json
+- Body: {"loginId": "username", "password": "password", "clientCode": "code"}
+- Response: {"nextGenCSO": "128-char-token", "loginResult": "0", "errorDescription": ""}
+
+## Party Search
+- POST to: https://pcl.uscourts.gov/pcl-public-api/rest/parties/find
+- Headers:
+  - Content-Type: application/json
+  - Accept: application/json
+  - X-NEXT-GEN-CSO: <token from auth>
+- Body:
+```json
+{
+  "lastName": "Smith",
+  "jurisdictionType": "bk",
+  "courtCase": {
+    "courtId": ["ganbk", "gasbk", "gambk"]
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## Key Points
+- 406 error means "invalid search parameter" or missing Accept header
+- The original code used basic auth instead of X-NEXT-GEN-CSO token
+- Must first authenticate, then use the token in headers
+- lastName is used for both person last names AND entity/business names
+- jurisdictionType "bk" limits to bankruptcy cases
+- Georgia bankruptcy courts: ganbk (Northern), gasbk (Southern), gambk (Middle)
